  "transcription_notes": [
   "removed vs base material: the edge SYN-SENT --CLOSE--> FIN-WAIT-1 in the predecessor transcription of this figure (see NOTICE) is NOT transcribed here: RFC 9293 Figure 5 draws no arrow from SYN-SENT into FIN-WAIT-1 (only SYN-RECEIVED and ESTABLISHED arrows enter FIN-WAIT-1), and sec.3.10.4 CLOSE Call, SYN-SENT STATE, says 'Delete the TCB and return \"error: closing\" responses to any queued SENDs, or RECEIVEs.' -- i.e. no transition to FIN-WAIT-1. Likely carried over from older RFC 793-style drawings.",
   "kept with changed citation: FIN-WAIT-1 --rcv FIN+FIN acked--> TIME-WAIT does not appear in the Figure 5 drawing; it is stated in sec.3.3.2 Note 2 ('The figure omits a transition from FIN-WAIT-1 to TIME-WAIT if a FIN is received and the local FIN is also acknowledged.') and is transcribed from Note 2. The event label 'rcv FIN+FIN acked' is the base material's shorthand for that wording, not an RFC-printed string.",
   "not collected (per the RFC's own omission): Note 3's any-state RST transitions (sending a RST goes to TIME-WAIT; receiving a RST goes to LISTEN or CLOSED) are omitted from Figure 5 'for legibility' and are not transcribed as model edges; only the drawn SYN-RECEIVED --rcv RST--> LISTEN edge (Note 1, conditional on having reached SYN-RECEIVED after a passive OPEN) is included.",
   "scope warning, quoted from the RFC: 'NOTA BENE: This diagram is only a summary and must not be taken as the total specification.' The model transcribes the diagram plus its Notes, not the full normative state machine of sections 3.5/3.10.",
   "encoding: states 11..15 are unreachable padding to reach 2^4 (engine input contract, same rule as the real 512/16,384-state cases); any (state, event) pair not listed in EDGES self-loops with reward 0 (undeclared event = no state change); rewards are all zero because TCP defines no payoff; goals is empty.",
   "names: the figure abbreviates state names (ESTAB, SYN RCVD, FIN WAIT-1, FINWAIT-2, CLOSE WAIT); this transcription uses the canonical state names, per RFC 9293's own remark that 'Some state names are abbreviated or hyphenated differently in the diagram from how they appear elsewhere in the document.'",
   "base material: a predecessor transcription of the same figure was used as the starting point (provenance and version pin in NOTICE); state numbering and event indices preserved; the SYN-SENT CLOSE edge removed (note 1); every edge re-verified against the RFC text on 2026-10-31."
  ],
  "regenerate": "python -X utf8 cases/tcp/make_tcp.py"
